#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-01.png", width: 361pt), 54pt, 11pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(561.82pt, 778.44pt, "1 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 15.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.24pt, 57.48pt, "Mechanisms of Zener diode and ohmic contact resulting from a heavily doped p-n ")
  #line-at(53.28pt, 75.84pt, "junction: A novel explanation in terms of impurity-photovoltaic-effect resulting ")
  #line-at(153.26pt, 94.22pt, "from infrared self-emission at room-temperature ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(271.25pt, 116.78pt, "Jianming Li ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(58.2pt, 142.94pt, "Institute of Semiconductors, Chinese Academy of Sciences, A35 Qinghua East Road, Haidian District, ")
  #line-at(237.05pt, 156.74pt, "Beijing 100083, P. R. China ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(99.264pt, 188.18pt, "ABSTRACT ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(99.264pt, 200.9pt, "In textbooks, a quantum-mechanical tunneling mechanism based on electron-wavefunction is ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 213.5pt, "used to explain Zener diode as well as ohmic contact resulting from a heavily doped p-n ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 226.1pt, "junction. In this study, an attempt in particle description is made to explain these devices. ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 238.82pt, "Any object at room-temperature emits infrared (IR) photons. The process of heavy doping ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 251.45pt, "can cause many defects. The self-absorption of the IR emission could be achieved through ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 264.05pt, "sub-band-gap excitations due to defects, creating carriers. In a heavily doped p-n junction ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 276.77pt, "device, some of the IR-generated carriers diffuse into the junction which has a built-in field. ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 289.37pt, "The built-in field sweeps out the carriers, creating IR photocurrent. The reverse leakage ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 301.97pt, "current of the p-n junction is regarded as the IR photocurrent according to a precedent where ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 314.69pt, "impurity-photovoltaic-effect is used to explain circuit devices (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(390.79pt, 314.69pt, "arXiv")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(415.27pt, 314.69pt, ":2510.18226). Heavy ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 327.29pt, "doping results in not only a great many IR-generated carriers but also an avalanche effect at ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 339.89pt, "low voltage, producing Zener breakdown. Additionally, the impurity-photovoltaic-effect can ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 352.61pt, "make a reasonable contribution to explaining the temperature dependence of Zener ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 365.21pt, "breakdown. If the doping is very heavy, the heavily doped p-n junction can be altered to ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 377.81pt, "create an ohmic contact, which can also be explained in terms of impurity-photovoltaic-")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 390.53pt, "effect. Not only quantum mechanics, but also this photovoltaic mechanism in particle ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 403.13pt, "description can explain the above devices. Considering the wave-particle duality, the ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 415.75pt, "combination of quantum-mechanical and photovoltaic mechanisms is suggested to explain ")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 428.47pt, "these devices. Each mechanism plays a big or small role in the explanation.")
  #set text(font: "SimSun", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 467.11pt, "Ⅰ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.52pt, 467.11pt, ". INTRODUCTION ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54.36pt, 480.67pt, "Diodes were discovered about a hundred years ago. At ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 493.27pt, "a breakdown voltage, the reverse current of a diode ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 505.87pt, "suddenly rises from an increasing reverse-bias voltage in ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 518.59pt, "which a very low dynamic resistance is present [1]. As ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 531.19pt, "shown in Fig. 1, Zener breakdown exists in a diode ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 543.79pt, "under reverse bias voltage (Vz), which was postulated ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 556.51pt, "by Zener in 1934 [2]. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 712.176pt, "Fig. 1. The current-voltage characteristics of a p-n junction ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 723.576pt, "diode. This schematic shows that an abrupt onset of reverse ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 735.096pt, "breakdown current occurs as applied voltage approaches ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 746.616pt, "breakdown value (Vz). ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(324.07pt, 466.27pt, "Zener diodes are one of the semiconductor diodes used ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 478.99pt, "in our daily life. A Zener diode has a well-controlled ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 491.59pt, "breakdown voltage and is used as a voltage regulator [3]. ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 504.19pt, "Zener diodes are a class of semiconductor diodes widely ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 516.91pt, "used for protection circuits, constant voltage circuits, ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 529.51pt, "level shift circuits, surge clippers etc.  ")
  #line-at(324.07pt, 542.11pt, "Under conditions of heavy doping, p-n junctions can ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 554.83pt, "be altered to Zener diodes or even ohmic contacts. In a ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 567.43pt, "tandem multi-junction solar cell, a reversed p–n junction ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 580.03pt, "exists between two cell p-n junctions. A challenge for ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 592.78pt, "tandem cells has been the development of the effectively ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 605.38pt, "electrical connection between the cell p-n junctions. ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 617.98pt, "Under conditions of very heavy doping, the reversed p-n ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 630.7pt, "junction can be altered to create an ohmic contact. ")
  #line-at(324.07pt, 643.3pt, "In textbooks, the theoretical understanding for both ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 655.9pt, "Zener diode and ohmic contact is quantum-mechanical ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 668.62pt, "tunneling based on electron-wavefunction [4]. Tunneling ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 681.22pt, "transmission is an example of wave-particle duality. In ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 693.816pt, "quantum mechanics, tunnelling is attributed to an ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 706.536pt, "electron wavefunction that extends into a potential ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 719.136pt, "barrier. As claimed in a textbook, “tunneling cannot be ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 731.736pt, "explained in the particle description, it requires the wave ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 744.456pt, "description” [5]. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(221.69pt, 24.48pt, "arXiv paper; Submitted on Nov. 9, 2026 ")
]

