#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-02.png", width: 441.5pt), 56pt, 54pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(561.7pt, 742.416pt, "2 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54.36pt, 59.88pt, "An attempt has been made to explain the ohmic ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 72.48pt, "contact of metal-semiconductor by using impurity-")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 85.1pt, "photovoltaic-effect in particle description [6]. In this ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 97.82pt, "study, the ohmic contact resulting from a heavily doped ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 110.42pt, "p-n junction is also explained in terms of impurity-")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 123.02pt, "photovoltaic-effect. ")
  #set text(font: "SimSun", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 149.18pt, "Ⅱ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.52pt, 149.18pt, ". SUPPOSED MECHANISM ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54.36pt, 162.62pt, "Since 2004, the impurity-photovoltaic-effect resulting ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 175.34pt, "from infrared self-emission at room-temperature has ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 187.94pt, "been proposed to create photocurrent in a p-n junction ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 200.54pt, "diode with unavoidable intrinsic background-defects ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 213.14pt, "[7,8].  ")
  #line-at(54.36pt, 225.86pt, "There is already a precedent where impurity-")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 238.46pt, "photovoltaic-effect is used to explain circuit devices [9]. ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 251.09pt, "Following the precedent, a mechanism based on ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 263.81pt, "impurity-photovoltaic-effect is supposed as follows. ")
  #line-at(55.32pt, 276.41pt, "As is well known, any object at room-temperature ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 289.01pt, "emits infrared (IR) photons due to blackbody radiation. ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 301.73pt, "Some ")
  #line-at(86.385pt, 301.73pt, "research ")
  #line-at(138.98pt, 301.73pt, "results ")
  #line-at(183.62pt, 301.73pt, "[10,11] ")
  #line-at(231.752pt, 301.73pt, "support ")
  #line-at(280.56pt, 301.73pt, "that ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 314.33pt, "semiconductor devices at room temperature emit IR ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 326.93pt, "photons. It is also known that heavy doping process can ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 339.65pt, "induce a lot of defects such as vacancies, interstitials, ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 352.25pt, "and imperfections associated with impurities, etc.  ")
  #line-at(54.36pt, 364.85pt, "In a heavily doped p-n junction diode, the defects ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 377.57pt, "create a lot of intermediate levels (bandgap states) in ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 390.17pt, "forbidden energy band-gap. The self-absorption of the ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 402.77pt, "IR emission within the diode could be achieved through ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 415.51pt, "the sub-band-gap excitations shown in Fig. 2, which ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 428.11pt, "produces a lot of electron–hole pairs. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 579.67pt, "Fig. 2. The sub-band-gap excitation mechanism via the ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 589.78pt, "intermediate levels within forbidden gap. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(55.2pt, 614.5pt, "As shown in Fig. 3(a), a depletion layer (a space-")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 627.22pt, "charge region with built-in electric field) exists in a p-n ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 639.82pt, "junction. Some of the IR-generated electrons and holes ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 652.42pt, "diffuse into the depletion layer where the electrons and ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 665.14pt, "holes drift in opposite directions due to the built-in field. ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 677.74pt, "Therefore, the p-n junction separates the IR-generated ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 690.34pt, "electrons and holes, producing IR photocurrent. A series ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 703.056pt, "of studies have shown that the reverse leakage current of ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 715.656pt, "a p-n junction is regarded as the IR photocurrent due to ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 728.256pt, "unavoidable intrinsic background-defects [7-9]. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(315.05pt, 361.01pt, "Fig. 3. A schematic of a p-n junction. (a) In thermodynamic ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 370.97pt, "equilibrium (without bias), (b) reverse bias, and (c) forward ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 380.93pt, "bias. W is depletion layer width.  ")
  #set text(font: "SimSun", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(315.05pt, 408.29pt, "Ⅲ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(326.23pt, 408.29pt, ". DISCUSSION ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(325.03pt, 421.75pt, "Comparing an ordinary diode, a Zener diode has ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 434.35pt, "higher doping concentration. Here, let us consider a p-n ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 447.07pt, "junction diode in which both p and n sides are heavily ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 459.67pt, "doped. Heavy doping results in a substantial gradient of ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 472.27pt, "carrier concentration in the depletion layer with a built-")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 484.99pt, "in electric field. ")
  #line-at(325.03pt, 497.59pt, "Under reverse bias, the applied voltage increases both ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 510.19pt, "the electric field and depletion layer width (W), as ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 522.91pt, "shown in Fig. 3(b), but the carrier diffusion length (L) ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 535.51pt, "out of the depletion layer remains unchanged. Thus, ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 548.11pt, "more IR-generated carriers created in and near the ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 560.83pt, "depletion layer can contribute to the IR reverse current. ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 573.43pt, "On the other hand, heavy doping itself creates a lot of ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 586.06pt, "defects, contributing to the creation of many IR-")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 598.78pt, "generated carriers due to the sub-band-gap excitations.  ")
  #line-at(325.03pt, 611.38pt, "As is known, impact-ionization occurs when a carrier ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 623.98pt, "gains sufficient energy from travelling in an electric-")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 636.7pt, "field to create an extra electron-hole pair. As this process ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 649.3pt, "continues it results in avalanche multiplication. ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 661.9pt, "Competing with impact-ionization process is energy loss ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 674.62pt, "by phonon emission [12-15]. ")
  #line-at(325.03pt, 687.22pt, "Heavy doping results in more IR-generated carriers, ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 699.816pt, "raising impact-ionization rate under the influence of the ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 712.536pt, "built-in field. Thus, the impurity-photovoltaic-effect in ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 725.136pt, "the heavily doped diode enables avalanche effect to ")
]

// arXiv source page 3
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(561.7pt, 742.416pt, "3 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 59.88pt, "occur at lower voltage, creating breakdown. In this way, ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 72.48pt, "Zener breakdown is explained in terms of impurity-")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 85.1pt, "photovoltaic-effect. ")
  #line-at(55.32pt, 97.82pt, "Similar to a research work which discusses the ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 110.42pt, "temperature dependence of tunneling diode [6], this ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 123.02pt, "study discusses the temperature dependence of Zener ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 135.74pt, "breakdown as follows. ")
  #line-at(55.32pt, 148.34pt, "For a low reverse-bias voltage regime, Zener ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 160.94pt, "breakdown voltage decreases as the temperature is raised, ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 173.66pt, "since the number of IR-generated carriers in the diode ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 186.26pt, "increases with increasing temperature. ")
  #line-at(55.32pt, 198.86pt, "On the other hand, for a greater reverse-bias voltage ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 211.58pt, "regime, the breakdown voltage increases as the ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 224.18pt, "temperature is raised, since raising temperature increases ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 236.78pt, "phonon scattering. In this process, the breakdown ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 249.53pt, "voltage is related to an increase in carrier scattering at ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 262.13pt, "elevated temperatures, and phonon scattering plays an ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 274.73pt, "important role. As the temperature increases phonon ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 287.45pt, "scattering increases, shortening carrier mean free path ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 300.05pt, "and thereby reducing the ionization coefficients. Thus, ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 312.65pt, "raising temperature increases the breakdown voltage for ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 325.37pt, "the greater bias voltage regime [16,17]. ")
  #line-at(55.32pt, 337.97pt, "If the doping is so heavy that a great many IR-")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 350.57pt, "generated carriers are created in the diode, the IR reverse ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 363.29pt, "current significantly increases with applied voltage even ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 375.89pt, "at low voltage range. In general, total reverse current ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 388.49pt, "dramatically increases with applied voltage. ")
  #line-at(55.32pt, 401.21pt, "In forward direction, the applied voltage decreases ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 413.83pt, "both W and built-in field, as shown in Fig. 3(c). Under ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 426.43pt, "the influence of substantial gradient of carrier ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 439.03pt, "concentration in the very heavily doped p-n junction ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 451.75pt, "diode, a strong forward diffuse current occurs. The ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 464.35pt, "forward diffuse current of the carriers significantly ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 476.95pt, "surpasses the reverse drift current of the IR-generated ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 489.67pt, "carriers. Therefore, total forward current dramatically ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 502.27pt, "increases with voltage. ")
  #line-at(55.32pt, 514.87pt, "According to the above mechanism based on ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 527.59pt, "impurity-photovoltaic-effect, the rectifying behavior of a ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 540.19pt, "p-n junction is lost under the condition of very heavy ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 552.79pt, "doping. Furthermore, the applied voltages make ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 565.51pt, "significant current flow occur in both forward and ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 578.11pt, "reverse current directions rather than in only one ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 590.74pt, "direction. Even at low applied voltages of either polarity, ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 603.46pt, "significant current flow occurs. Such p-n junction has a ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 616.06pt, "small contact resistance in both current directions, ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 628.66pt, "creating an ohmic contact. ")
  #line-at(55.32pt, 641.38pt, "In principle, the impurity-photovoltaic-effect applies ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 653.98pt, "to the explanation for heavily doped p-n junctions in all ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 666.58pt, "kinds of semiconductor materials. ")
  #set text(font: "SimSun", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 692.736pt, "Ⅳ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.52pt, 692.736pt, ". CONCLUSIONS ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54.72pt, 706.176pt, "In general, both Zener diode and ohmic contact ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 718.776pt, "resulting from a heavily doped p-n junction can be ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 59.88pt, "indeed explained by using the mechanism based on ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 72.48pt, "impurity-photovoltaic-effect in particle description. Not ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 85.1pt, "only quantum mechanics, but also the photovoltaic ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 97.82pt, "mechanism in particle description can explain these ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 110.42pt, "devices. This study provides a reasonable support for the ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 123.02pt, "mechanism of impurity-photovoltaic-effect due to IR ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 135.74pt, "absorption. Quantum mechanics is a great discipline and ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 148.34pt, "provides an effective description of electrons in view of ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 160.94pt, "wave. ")
  #line-at(357.377pt, 160.94pt, "Considering ")
  #line-at(427.537pt, 160.94pt, "wave-particle ")
  #line-at(503.835pt, 160.94pt, "duality, ")
  #line-at(553.372pt, 160.94pt, "the ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 173.66pt, "combination of quantum-mechanical tunneling and ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 186.26pt, "impurity-photovoltaic-effect mechanisms is suggested to ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 198.86pt, "explain the above devices. Each of the two mechanisms ")
  #line-at(315.05pt, 211.58pt, "plays a big or small role in the explanation. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
